      "value": "@{5ca74f3fb98a820b3ffec9cf|full_name}: I found them, but my impression is that \"Lock Head\" is the only setting which behaves acceptably. The other two might as well be deleted from the client unless someone can provide a reasonable explanation of why I would want it to behave incorrectly. I tried \"Lock Head\" just now, and it even made the legs move better than \"Lock Hips\" was managing.\n\nDiscoverability is also a UX thing and something which VRChat could work on. I discovered these settings only when some other user told me about them after I had made an angry post on a ticket. One could easily argue that this isn't the ideal way for a user to discover that a feature exists. It certainly wasn't ever mentioned during the onboarding tutorial - instead the tutorial wastes its time talking about other things which I don't care about.\n\nAnd I still maintain that, the default setting should be the one that works correctly. So regardless of the fact that \"Lock Head\" seems to have fixed it for me (for now, at least until next time they change the IK), the default was still wrong and VRChat should still feel bad about having the wrong default.\n\nSo at a minimum:\n\n1) The default is wrong;\n\n2) It's a setting where only one out of the three options even behaves correctly and therefore should be considered for deletion; and\n\n3) Closing tickets without people verifying that the issue is fixed is still shittty behaviour from any company, including VRChat.\n\nNote that A could well have mentioned the existence of this setting when marking the ticket as resolved - this did not happen at all. And \"the post is quite old\" is still not an acceptable reason for closing a ticket, as I already explained in detail on Twitter.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
